[{"id":126190,"sender_id":43,"sender_full_name":"DavidRoberts","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/fbc2dbfb28f9e9275a4fd4cd109b5a21?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/plus.20construction.20on.20presheaves/near/126190\">#17</a> I have a memory that there is a reference that gives the result explicitly that a presheaf of categories is turned into a stack by three applications of +. But I’m having trouble turning it up. I don’t mean as a version of Lurie, but say Street or Giraud or Grothendieck.</p>","timestamp":1791361861,"subject":"plus construction on presheaves","stream_id":2,"display_recipient":"Latest Changes","reactions":[]},{"id":126205,"sender_id":43,"sender_full_name":"DavidRoberts","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/fbc2dbfb28f9e9275a4fd4cd109b5a21?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/2-Latest-Changes/topic/plus.20construction.20on.20presheaves/near/126205\">#18</a> OK, it’s in Street’s <em>Two-dimensional Sheaf Theory</em>, using <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">L</span></span></span></span> for <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(-)^+</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0213em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mclose\"><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7713em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">+</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>. A prestack is described as a presheaf where the comparison functor to descent data is representably fully faithful and <em>injective on objects</em>, which is clearly not equivalence-invariant. Not actually itself injective on objects, but inducing such a 1-arrow on the map of representable presheaves on Cat. But at a brief glance it’s the thing you expect.</p>","timestamp":1791626650,"subject":"plus construction on presheaves","stream_id":2,"display_recipient":"Latest Changes","reactions":[]}]